+\textbf{R1. What is predicted, and when?} A camera can supply a predictor or a reference measured after the event. For each study, we identify the physical event, when each observation was available, and how the target was obtained. In PHM, post-run photographs supply a proxy for gear condition. In REASSEMBLE, the camera and sensors are predictors paired with a recorded action outcome.
+
+\textbf{R2. What does each representation retain (SQ1)?} Published results for engineered features, pretrained visual features and temporal patches concern different targets and fitting conditions \parencite{horwitz_back_2023,roth_towards_2022,nie_time_2023}. We compare individual branches on the same target and observation window, recording their training histories and fitting budgets. A branch's standalone score leaves open whether it contributes information to another predictor.
+
+\textbf{R3. What does fusion add (SQ2)?} The clean welding tie and the loss after adding gripper state in handover make the strongest single input an essential comparator \parencite{hua_anti-interference_2026,thoduka_multimodal_2024}. On the 4,530 eligible REASSEMBLE actions, we compare camera and sensor predictions, fixed averaging and fitted combinations with the same recordings held out. The feature-level model F3 projects a 128-dimensional visual representation and 220 sensor statistics to two 128-dimensional vectors and concatenates them. This is distinct from combining two representations of the sensor stream. Chapter~\ref{ch:reassemble} gives the fitting and calibration differences that limit attribution to the fusion rule alone.
+
+\textbf{R4. Which reliability condition is being tested (SQ3)?} Knowing an input is absent calls for a different response from receiving a degraded but apparently available signal \parencite{deng_tc-maf_2026,zhang_provable_2023}. We identify the affected input and what the model knows about its condition. In the matched REASSEMBLE comparison, static and adaptive models receive comparable corruption exposure during fitting. Both are assessed on clean and corrupted cases. Timing changes and transfer to another domain are separate tests.
+
+\textbf{R5. How dependable is the comparison (SQ4)?} Selection on related observations can inflate performance estimates \parencite{varma_bias_2006,kapoor_leakage_2023}. The assessment unit follows the acquisition process, such as a gear experiment, recording, or manipulation task. Ranking, probability calibration and uncertainty answer different questions about failure prediction. Across datasets, we distinguish refitting a procedure, transferring representation weights and testing an unchanged predictor. Table~\ref{tab:fusion-study-scope} identifies which of these claims the available data support.
